# Adept Watershaper: "Other tapped creatures you control have indestructible." Bot1 attacks on turn 3 with Adept Watershaper and
# one of two Ornithopters and Bot2 attacks with its Elves on turn 4, all of them tapped still. The attacking Ornithopter is tapped and so indestructible (CR 702.12, 613.1f); the untapped one, the
# tapped Watershaper itself ("other") and Bot2's tapped Llanowar Elves ("you control") are not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Adept Watershaper
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Adept Watershaper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Adept Watershaper; Ornithopter#1 > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Adept Watershaper.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Adept Watershaper.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Keywords = Flying; Indestructible
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Keywords = Flying
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = (absent)
